---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import biography from "../biography.json";

const fact = Object.fromEntries(biography.facts.map((item) => [item.id, item.value]));
---

<Base
  title="Filipe Fantini — ofantini.com"
  description="Filipe Fantini designs and builds data platforms, from ingestion to the people who run them. Lagom is a personal laboratory, not an employer's system."
  canonical="https://ofantini.com/"
  current="home"
  inventory="biography"
>
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Personal</p>
      <h1 transition:name="title">Platforms, built and handed on.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I am a data engineering lead with {fact.years} of designing and building platforms end to
        end: ingestion, modelling, governance, BI and AI enablement. This site is that work, in my
        own words. The laboratory is a separate page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage stage-3d" aria-label="On the bench">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker stage-label">On the bench</p>
      <ul class="pieces">
        <li>
          <a class="piece piece-work" href="#work">
            <span class="piece-name">The work</span>
            <span class="piece-line">Envision, Enhesa, and the years before.</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="piece piece-standards" href="#standards">
            <span class="piece-name">The standard</span>
            <span class="piece-line">Reliability, and a roadmap a business can use.</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="piece piece-lab" href="/projects">
            <span class="piece-name">The laboratory</span>
            <span class="piece-line">Lagom. Not an employer's system.</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="era era-now" id="work">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Now</p>
      <h2>Envision Pharma Group</h2>
      <p>
        Since {fact["envision-when"]}, in {fact["envision-place"]}, I lead the data engineering
        team and own platform direction on Snowflake, dbt and Fivetran: architecture, roadmap and
        delivery. Ingestion and dbt modelling are scaling with a layered project structure —
        staging, intermediate, marts — with testing and documentation conventions, and cost-aware
        warehouse usage. Governance, lineage and DataOps are how reliability, data quality and cost
        stay in the same conversation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="era era-enhesa">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Before that</p>
      <h2>Enhesa</h2>
      <p>
        From {fact["enhesa-span"]}, in {fact["enhesa-place"]}, I was Business Intelligence Manager,
        promoted from BI Engineer in {fact.promoted}. I designed and delivered the company's cloud
        data platform on Microsoft Fabric and Azure: a medallion architecture, Bronze, Silver and
        Gold, built on Spark, which became the single source of truth for analytics. I led the move
        off SSRS and Azure Synapse.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pipelines with Fivetran, Azure Data Factory and Spark crossed {fact.sources} — databases,
        APIs, SaaS and files — processing {fact.records}. Reverse ETL with Census pushed curated
        data back into business tools. Kimball models, slowly changing dimensions and conformed
        dimensions, feed {fact["semantic-models"]}, with row-level security and incremental refresh.
      </p>
      <p>
        I introduced Git-based CI/CD on Azure DevOps, mandatory code reviews, layer and naming
        conventions, data quality checks, documentation and lineage. An MCP-based data assistant,
        built with Claude, is used company-wide by hundreds of employees to query data in natural
        language, with access restricted to the curated Gold layer. I led {fact.team} of data
        engineers and BI developers, {fact["team-scaled"]} for project demand, and developed an
        integration developer into a Senior Data Engineer based on delivery.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="era era-early">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Earlier</p>
      <h2>Brazil, {fact["earlier-span"]}</h2>
      <p>
        Data Analyst, Sales Operations, at LinkedIn in {fact["linkedin-year"]}, using Power BI, SQL
        and ETL. Before that, Data Analyst and BI Intern at Padtec, {fact["earlier-span"]}, with
        ETL in Python and Pentaho, SQL Server, Power BI and SSRS.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pull" id="standards">
    <div class="wrap">
      <blockquote>
        I hire and grow engineers, set the standards that keep platforms reliable, and partner with
        business leaders to turn priorities into delivered value.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        The tools named on the CV are Snowflake, Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Factory, Azure
        Synapse, Azure Blob Storage, dbt, Fivetran, Census, Apache Spark, PySpark, SQL, Python and
        Power BI, with Kimball modelling, CI/CD and access control around them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="era" id="study">
    <div class="wrap study">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Study</p>
        <h2>Still in the tools.</h2>
        <p>
          Postgraduate study in Complex Data Mining at UNICAMP, {fact.unicamp}, in progress. A
          bachelor's degree in Mechatronics and Robotics from UNISAL, {fact.unisal}.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Certificate and languages</p>
        <h2>{fact.dp600}</h2>
        <p>Microsoft Fabric Analytics Engineer. Portuguese is native. English is fluent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
